1. Probe: read the ID register
  i2c: S 2A+W A 00 A Sr 2A+R A A5 N P
   ID = 0xA5 (expected 0xA5)
2. Configure: accel range index 1 (+-4 g), gyro range index 1 (+-500 dps)
  i2c: S 2A+W A 10 A 05 A P
3. One raw read of 12 data bytes
  i2c: S 2A+W A 20 A Sr 2A+R A 07 A 55 A 0F A F8 A 1B A 6D A 00 A 32 A FF A E5 A 00 A 06 N P
   AZ bytes 1B 6D -> 7021 counts -> 0.8571 g
   (bytes swapped by mistake -> 27931 counts -> 3.4095 g)
4. Calibrate gyro bias: average 200 samples while not moving
   gyro bias estimate: +0.803 -0.349 +0.098 dps (model truth +0.80 -0.35 +0.10)
5. Tilt from the averaged accelerometer
   accel mean: +0.1732 +0.4927 +0.8510 g, length 0.9984 g
   roll 30.07 deg (truth 30.0), pitch -9.99 deg (truth -10.0)
6. A read from the wrong address
  i2c: S 2B+W N P
   no acknowledge: report an error, do not hang
